WEBVTT

00:01.835 --> 00:04.713
Satoru, take him to the dorm.

00:04.796 --> 00:08.091
Also, explain the various
security measures to him.

00:08.174 --> 00:09.217
What?

00:10.635 --> 00:11.970
You've passed.

00:12.053 --> 00:14.180
Welcome to Jujutsu High School.

00:15.473 --> 00:16.808
Fushiguro!

00:16.891 --> 00:18.852
You definitely look much better this time.

00:18.935 --> 00:21.146
There are plenty of empty rooms.

00:21.229 --> 00:23.565
Isn't it better
when the place is more lively?

00:23.648 --> 00:26.484
-I think it's good--
-Just classes and missions are sufficient.

00:26.568 --> 00:27.527
What a pain…

00:27.610 --> 00:30.363
Oh, wow! Your room looks really tidy!

00:30.447 --> 00:33.992
-Like I said, you're a bother!
-Oh, god!

00:34.075 --> 00:36.244
But isn't this fine?

00:36.327 --> 00:38.455
Anyway, we're going out tomorrow!

00:38.538 --> 00:42.041
We'll be meeting
the third first-year student.

00:45.587 --> 00:51.718
The Shibuya-Shinagawa train
will be arriving on Platform 1 soon.

00:52.427 --> 00:56.306
For your own safety,
please stand behind the yellow line.

00:57.015 --> 00:58.308
Saori…

01:00.643 --> 01:02.187
I'm here.

01:07.567 --> 01:08.943
I'm in Tokyo.

01:10.779 --> 01:13.823
There are only three first-year students.
Isn't that too few?

01:13.907 --> 01:18.453
Well, have you ever seen a man
who could see a curse before?

01:18.536 --> 01:19.954
Well…

01:20.038 --> 01:20.955
No.

01:21.039 --> 01:24.459
And that's why
there are very few Jujutsu Sorcerers.

01:24.542 --> 01:27.295
By the way,
I thought I was the third student.

01:27.378 --> 01:30.465
I heard that her school transfer
was decided way back.

01:31.216 --> 01:32.967
It's a special school after all.

01:33.551 --> 01:35.386
She must have had a reason.

01:37.013 --> 01:39.224
Sorry to keep you waiting! What?

01:40.099 --> 01:41.768
So your school uniform came in time.

01:41.851 --> 01:43.645
Yes, it fits me perfectly!

01:43.728 --> 01:45.939
But it looks
slightly different from Fushiguro's.

01:46.022 --> 01:47.774
It even has a hood.

01:47.857 --> 01:51.069
The uniform can be altered upon request.

01:51.152 --> 01:51.986
What?

01:52.070 --> 01:54.614
I didn't ask for that.

01:54.697 --> 01:57.742
That's because
I made a custom request for you.

01:57.826 --> 01:59.119
I see.

01:59.619 --> 02:01.079
Oh, well, it's fine.

02:01.162 --> 02:04.624
Be careful. This is Mr. Gojo's habit.

02:05.416 --> 02:08.002
By the way,
why are we meeting in Harajuku?

02:08.086 --> 02:10.088
She said she wanted to meet here.

02:10.171 --> 02:12.507
I want popcorn!

02:13.091 --> 02:15.677
Hello. Are you working now?

02:15.760 --> 02:17.428
No, I'm not.

02:17.512 --> 02:20.098
I'm looking for a model.

02:20.181 --> 02:22.016
That's my job.

02:22.100 --> 02:23.768
Are you interested in becoming one?

02:23.852 --> 02:25.311
I'm in a hurry.

02:25.395 --> 02:27.480
Let's just have a talk!

02:29.315 --> 02:31.192
Hey, you.

02:31.276 --> 02:32.569
What about me?

02:33.444 --> 02:34.863
"What about me?"

02:35.655 --> 02:39.617
I'm asking about the modeling job.
What do you think about me?

02:39.701 --> 02:42.370
Oh, you know, I'm in a hurry.

02:44.539 --> 02:47.667
What the heck?
Don't run away. Make it clear!

02:47.750 --> 02:51.713
-Are we going to talk to that now?
-Excuse me, please forgive me!

02:51.796 --> 02:53.631
I'm getting a little embarrassed.

02:53.715 --> 02:55.884
The same goes for you too.

02:55.967 --> 02:57.844
Hey, over here!

02:57.927 --> 03:00.930
Oh, my! What's with
the guy with the blindfold?

03:04.434 --> 03:06.227
Let's do the introduction again.

03:07.061 --> 03:08.771
My name is Nobara Kugisaki.

03:08.855 --> 03:11.900
Cheer up, boys. Here comes a girl.

04:43.032 --> 04:47.912
Stare…

04:47.996 --> 04:51.124
The name's Yuji Itadori. I'm from Sendai.

04:51.207 --> 04:52.667
I'm Megumi Fushiguro.

04:54.252 --> 04:56.296
How crude.

04:56.379 --> 04:59.257
He's definitely that kid
who used to eat his own boogers.

04:59.340 --> 05:01.342
Judging by his name, he sounds like

05:01.426 --> 05:04.095
someone full of himself.
I can't deal with boys like him.

05:04.679 --> 05:07.890
He's the kind that will ignite a fire
on oil-drenched seagulls.

05:08.433 --> 05:09.684
Man.

05:09.767 --> 05:12.603
I've got a real mess on my hands.

05:12.687 --> 05:15.315
She's sighing after seeing our faces.

05:15.398 --> 05:17.108
Are we headed somewhere after this?

05:18.526 --> 05:21.070
It's rare for the three
first-year students to gather.

05:21.154 --> 05:24.115
And two of them just came to Tokyo.

05:24.198 --> 05:25.533
Of course, we're going to…

05:25.616 --> 05:27.118
do some sightseeing in Tokyo.

05:27.201 --> 05:30.288
-Tokyo!
-Tokyo!

05:30.371 --> 05:32.373
-We love Tokyo!
-What?

05:32.457 --> 05:34.417
I want to go to Tokyo Disneyland!

05:34.500 --> 05:36.377
You dumbass! Tokyo Disneyland's in Chiba!

05:36.461 --> 05:40.089
-Let's go to Chinatown, Mr. Gojo.
-Chinatown is in Yokohama!

05:40.173 --> 05:44.052
Isn't Yokohama in Tokyo?
Don't you know? Look at the map!

05:44.135 --> 05:47.388
-What? Don't be ridiculous.
-Allow me to announce the destination.

05:47.472 --> 05:50.391
It's Roppongi!

05:50.475 --> 05:52.894
-Roppongi.
-Roppongi.

05:55.521 --> 05:57.231
There's a curse here, isn't there?

05:57.857 --> 05:59.275
-You liar!
-You liar!

05:59.358 --> 06:00.735
This is Roppongi, right?

06:00.818 --> 06:02.528
How dare you mock countryside folks!

06:03.237 --> 06:05.323
There's a big cemetery nearby.

06:05.823 --> 06:09.035
Add dilapidated buildings to the mix,
and curses start to appear.

06:09.118 --> 06:11.746
Isn't it easier for them
to appear in cemeteries?

06:12.622 --> 06:14.540
The problem is not the cemetery.

06:14.624 --> 06:18.920
It's the heart of those
who think the cemetery is terrible.

06:19.003 --> 06:21.547
Oh, just like that time in school.

06:21.631 --> 06:24.550
Wait, this guy doesn't even know that?

06:25.134 --> 06:26.010
Actually…

06:28.888 --> 06:31.557
He ate the Special Grade Cursed Relic?

06:31.641 --> 06:33.726
It's so disgusting!

06:33.810 --> 06:35.144
How unhygienic!

06:35.228 --> 06:36.562
No way!

06:36.646 --> 06:37.772
What did you say?

06:37.855 --> 06:38.815
I agree with that.

06:38.898 --> 06:41.442
I want to know everyone's skill level.

06:41.526 --> 06:44.070
This will serve as a practical test.

06:44.153 --> 06:48.116
Nobara and Yuji.
Get rid of the curse in this building.

06:48.199 --> 06:49.117
What?

06:49.617 --> 06:53.329
What? Didn't you say that
a curse can only be exorcised by a curse?

06:53.412 --> 06:55.581
I don't know how to cast a curse.

06:55.665 --> 06:58.835
You're already half a curse.

06:58.918 --> 07:01.087
You have cursed energy in your body.

07:01.170 --> 07:05.091
However, you can't
just control curses easily.

07:05.174 --> 07:06.509
So use this instead.

07:08.553 --> 07:10.638
This is a Cursed Tool
known as Slaughter Demon.

07:10.721 --> 07:12.390
It's a weapon with cursed energy.

07:12.473 --> 07:14.892
It works on curses too.

07:15.476 --> 07:16.561
How lame!

07:19.439 --> 07:21.732
-Oh, also…
-What?

07:21.816 --> 07:24.110
You can't release Sukuna.

07:25.361 --> 07:28.614
Letting him out
will get rid of the curse immediately,

07:28.698 --> 07:31.200
but it will implicate
the humans nearby as well.

07:31.284 --> 07:33.703
Got it. I won't let him out.

07:35.455 --> 07:36.789
Hurry up!

07:36.873 --> 07:37.832
Okay.

07:37.915 --> 07:39.041
Have a safe trip.

07:51.262 --> 07:52.889
Should I follow them?

07:52.972 --> 07:56.184
Don't force it, you just recovered.

07:56.267 --> 07:58.478
But I think we need
to keep an eye on Itadori.

07:59.187 --> 08:00.104
True.

08:00.605 --> 08:04.567
-But it's Nobara we're testing this time.
-What?

08:04.650 --> 08:06.110
It's depressing.

08:06.194 --> 08:09.572
Why are we still fighting curses in Tokyo?

08:09.655 --> 08:10.490
What?

08:10.573 --> 08:12.533
Aren't you here to get rid of curses?

08:12.617 --> 08:14.035
This is a waste of time.

08:14.118 --> 08:15.453
Let's split up.

08:15.536 --> 08:18.206
I'll start from the top
and work my way down.

08:18.289 --> 08:19.540
You start from the bottom.

08:19.624 --> 08:22.543
Let's finish this up quick
and head to Ginza for sushi.

08:22.627 --> 08:25.546
Wait a minute. Let's be serious.

08:25.630 --> 08:27.632
Curses are dangerous.

08:30.843 --> 08:33.930
I don't want a newbie
to comment on my work!

08:34.013 --> 08:35.306
Just hurry up and go!

08:37.141 --> 08:40.102
I don't get your attitude at all!

08:40.186 --> 08:42.063
That's why you're not popular with girls!

08:42.146 --> 08:45.024
How did you know that?

08:45.107 --> 08:47.527
Are you so popular that you can say that?

08:47.610 --> 08:48.778
Darn it!

08:50.613 --> 08:51.531
What?

08:58.788 --> 09:02.875
Here is your receipt…

09:05.086 --> 09:06.087
A curse has appeared.

09:27.567 --> 09:28.734
All right.

09:29.610 --> 09:31.112
I can move well.

09:32.655 --> 09:36.325
Yuji's quite the crazy person.

09:36.409 --> 09:37.868
Even if they look horrendous,

09:37.952 --> 09:40.204
or if they take after human forms,

09:40.288 --> 09:42.915
as long as they're trying to kill him,

09:42.999 --> 09:45.459
he will destroy it without hesitation.

09:47.461 --> 09:51.382
Unlike you, he wasn't exposed to curses
at a young age.

09:51.465 --> 09:55.386
He's a boy who lived
a normal high school life.

09:56.345 --> 10:00.099
Even with talent,
there are Jujutsu Sorcerers

10:00.182 --> 10:03.311
unable to conquer their fear
and disgust of destroying these monsters.

10:03.394 --> 10:05.354
I'm sure you've seen
your fair share, right?

10:07.481 --> 10:10.943
I want to confirm her insanity today.

10:12.486 --> 10:14.697
Hey, that curse over there.

10:20.494 --> 10:22.788
I'm talking to you,
the dummy in the middle.

10:22.872 --> 10:24.957
Do you think you can hide from me?

10:28.002 --> 10:30.379
If you don't come over, I'll destroy you.

10:30.880 --> 10:33.424
But Kugisaki is experienced, right?

10:33.507 --> 10:35.092
How will this help?

10:35.593 --> 10:38.304
A curse is born from people's hearts.

10:38.387 --> 10:42.266
It also grows stronger
in proportion to our population.

10:52.860 --> 10:53.778
Okay.

11:01.035 --> 11:03.079
Can Nobara understand this?

11:05.247 --> 11:09.585
The curse level between
the countryside and Tokyo is different.

11:11.003 --> 11:13.422
KUGISAKI RESIDENCE

11:18.135 --> 11:20.513
A curse is born from people's hearts.

11:20.596 --> 11:21.430
GO BACK TO TOKYO

11:21.514 --> 11:25.017
It also grows stronger
in proportion to our population.

11:26.227 --> 11:30.356
The curse level between
the countryside and Tokyo is different.

11:38.322 --> 11:40.616
I suggest you take those out.

11:46.038 --> 11:48.707
Since my curse flows into them.

11:56.215 --> 11:57.633
All done.

12:09.812 --> 12:11.230
There's a child.

12:11.814 --> 12:15.443
He probably sneaked in here to play
and got caught by the curse.

12:18.696 --> 12:20.948
Come on, it's fine now.

12:21.782 --> 12:22.950
Come out.

12:24.535 --> 12:25.911
What?

12:29.832 --> 12:34.044
So it's true that kids
won't go near pretty girls.

12:34.128 --> 12:35.254
I'll call Itadori.

12:35.337 --> 12:36.338
Wait!

12:37.840 --> 12:39.341
Don't leave me.

12:58.569 --> 12:59.987
Is it using him as a hostage?

13:01.530 --> 13:04.158
This curse has intelligence.

13:04.241 --> 13:05.743
Even if there are levels,

13:05.826 --> 13:08.454
they are not based
solely on their curse level.

13:08.537 --> 13:09.371
What?

13:09.455 --> 13:10.539
"Deviousness."

13:10.623 --> 13:14.960
Beasts with intelligence
may occasionally set a cruel scale.

13:15.878 --> 13:19.215
With life on a scale, that is.

13:19.840 --> 13:21.175
Darn it.

13:21.258 --> 13:23.177
Darn it!

13:23.260 --> 13:26.430
This curse is nothing to me.

13:26.514 --> 13:29.099
It's a Grade 4. Or even a Grade 3.

13:29.183 --> 13:30.392
The lowest of the lowest!

13:31.727 --> 13:37.358
It knows that,
and that's why it's taking hostages.

13:38.859 --> 13:40.402
I need to calm down.

13:41.278 --> 13:44.865
If I die, that child will die too.

13:45.366 --> 13:48.494
Even if the child dies first, I won't die.

13:50.412 --> 13:52.248
Think reasonably.

13:52.748 --> 13:54.792
Even if it's just me…

13:55.292 --> 13:57.461
I guess it's worth it
to save a life, right?

14:03.050 --> 14:04.218
I'm unarmed.

14:04.843 --> 14:06.512
Let him go.

14:12.810 --> 14:14.520
I'm such an idiot.

14:15.062 --> 14:17.773
See? It's not letting him go.

14:22.236 --> 14:25.698
I wanted to meet Saori for the last time.

14:29.743 --> 14:31.787
Wait, I missed?

14:44.758 --> 14:46.343
Are you okay?

14:46.427 --> 14:47.720
Yes.

14:50.598 --> 14:51.765
It's running away!

14:51.849 --> 14:54.518
I'm not letting you run!
Itadori, give that hand to me!

14:54.602 --> 14:55.436
What?

14:57.521 --> 14:58.397
What?

14:58.480 --> 15:00.024
-I'll exorcise it.
-Don't panic.

15:02.067 --> 15:03.360
A voodoo doll?

15:03.444 --> 15:04.445
It's too dark.

15:08.032 --> 15:09.658
Straw Doll Technique…

15:11.493 --> 15:12.745
Resonance!

15:21.712 --> 15:24.465
Nice. She is crazy.

15:29.887 --> 15:31.138
We won.

15:38.020 --> 15:41.941
DUE TO CORROSION AND POTENTIAL DANGER,
THIS BRIDGE IS OUT OF SERVICE

15:47.863 --> 15:49.823
During my first year in elementary school,

15:51.200 --> 15:53.911
Saori moved to our village from Tokyo.

15:58.666 --> 16:00.084
What?

16:06.507 --> 16:09.927
Saori looked as cute as a doll,

16:10.594 --> 16:13.555
and was gentle like the Virgin Mary.

16:15.015 --> 16:17.935
STICKER BOOK

16:22.022 --> 16:26.819
However, she was ostracized
by the villagers.

16:30.864 --> 16:32.992
They said she mocked us countryside folks.

16:33.492 --> 16:36.412
They were so delusional.

16:37.329 --> 16:38.414
And so…

16:42.501 --> 16:44.211
They chased Saori out of the village.

16:44.294 --> 16:47.423
PROPERTY FOR SALE

16:47.506 --> 16:49.967
They are all disgusting.

16:50.050 --> 16:51.427
GARBAGE
GO BACK TO TOKYO

16:54.763 --> 16:57.683
Saori treated me to handmade snacks
I had never even heard of,

16:57.766 --> 17:02.813
smiled and said to me,
"The ones from the shops taste better."

17:07.067 --> 17:11.030
If I stayed in that village, I would have…

17:13.532 --> 17:14.950
Didn't I tell you?

17:15.034 --> 17:17.411
It's dangerous to travel alone,
so take it seriously.

17:17.494 --> 17:20.247
You didn't say
it was dangerous to go alone!

17:20.330 --> 17:21.957
Didn't I say that?

17:22.041 --> 17:23.667
Anyway, what did you eat growing up

17:23.751 --> 17:25.878
to break through
a wall with your bare hands?

17:25.961 --> 17:28.255
It's because there are
no steel reinforcement bars!

17:28.338 --> 17:30.966
Even without those,
a normal person couldn't have done it!

17:32.176 --> 17:33.927
What do you mean by "normal person"?

17:34.678 --> 17:38.015
By the way, I've been asked before…

17:38.098 --> 17:40.350
But why did you come
to Jujutsu High School?

17:40.434 --> 17:41.852
Why, you ask me?

17:42.978 --> 17:46.857
Because I hate the countryside
and I want to live in Tokyo!

17:46.940 --> 17:48.484
What?

17:50.444 --> 17:54.948
This is the only way to get to Tokyo
without worrying about the cost.

17:55.032 --> 17:57.618
You would actually risk your life
for that reason?

18:00.537 --> 18:02.081
Of course.

18:02.164 --> 18:03.165
What?

18:06.085 --> 18:08.212
I live for myself.

18:12.049 --> 18:15.344
If I stayed in that village,
I would be as good as dead.

18:25.229 --> 18:29.149
Saori, I'm in Tokyo.

18:34.113 --> 18:35.322
If we meet again,

18:36.573 --> 18:40.160
be sure to take me
to the shop you mentioned.

18:45.082 --> 18:48.544
I'm thankful to you.

18:48.627 --> 18:51.755
Even if I died or survived alone,

18:51.839 --> 18:53.841
I would never have a bright future.

18:54.967 --> 18:55.843
Thank you.

18:56.677 --> 18:57.803
Well…

18:57.886 --> 19:00.973
It's not like having a serious reason
makes it sound more remarkable.

19:01.056 --> 19:03.725
All right! Since I’ve thanked you,
we're even now!

19:03.809 --> 19:05.644
I don't owe you anything!

19:05.727 --> 19:07.354
What's wrong with her?

19:08.605 --> 19:11.358
My house is just up ahead. Thank you!

19:14.444 --> 19:17.489
Do you know that I get grumpy
when I'm hungry?

19:17.573 --> 19:19.825
Is there any time where you're not grumpy?

19:21.118 --> 19:23.912
-Good work, you guys!
-What?

19:23.996 --> 19:25.747
The child has reached home safely.

19:27.624 --> 19:29.376
Let's go eat for real now.

19:30.377 --> 19:33.005
-Steak!
-Sushi!

19:34.131 --> 19:35.841
Just leave it to me!

19:35.924 --> 19:36.967
What about you, Megumi?

19:39.428 --> 19:40.470
What?

19:40.554 --> 19:42.556
-Well then, let's go.
-Hey.

19:45.392 --> 19:46.351
Hey.

19:46.435 --> 19:48.937
I forgot the biggest gain of the day.

19:49.021 --> 19:51.356
You, help me get my luggage.

19:51.440 --> 19:52.274
What?

19:52.357 --> 19:55.194
Why should I? I thought we're even now.

19:55.277 --> 19:58.197
It was my curse that defeated it.
Is there any problem?

19:58.280 --> 20:00.407
You don't know
what I'm capable of, do you?

20:00.490 --> 20:02.868
You eat gross stuff
and have nothing but muscles.

20:02.951 --> 20:04.369
It's more than that!

20:04.453 --> 20:05.829
Right, Fushiguro?

20:06.997 --> 20:08.790
What's wrong, Fushiguro?

20:08.874 --> 20:09.708
Nothing.

20:09.791 --> 20:11.668
He's angry because he didn't get to play.

20:11.752 --> 20:14.171
How childish!

20:21.929 --> 20:27.851
Record, July 2018,
Eishu Detention Center, West Tokyo City.

20:30.437 --> 20:33.357
Above the stadium.

20:35.442 --> 20:36.610
Hey.

20:37.945 --> 20:39.363
What's that?

20:40.656 --> 20:41.615
Let me see.

20:42.199 --> 20:45.410
Special Grade Imaginary Cursed Spirit,
name unidentified.

20:46.119 --> 20:50.415
Several non-sorcerers
witnessed the Cursed Womb.

20:50.958 --> 20:53.418
That one. It looks like an egg.

20:53.502 --> 20:55.045
Like I said, where is it?

20:56.672 --> 21:01.134
In response to this emergency,
three first-year students were dispatched.

21:01.969 --> 21:04.388
One casualty reported.

22:35.937 --> 22:38.148
-Juju Stroll!
-Juju Stroll!

22:38.231 --> 22:40.650
I'll use paper, Itadori.

22:41.735 --> 22:43.653
Rock, paper, scissors!

22:43.737 --> 22:44.780
All right!

22:44.863 --> 22:47.574
Are we eating sushi?
Let's go to the usual place in Ginza.

22:47.657 --> 22:49.785
Ginza, all right!

22:49.868 --> 22:51.286
I want to have sushi train.

22:51.369 --> 22:52.287
What?

22:52.370 --> 22:54.122
You're hopeless, Itadori.

22:54.206 --> 22:55.791
Say something too, Fushiguro!

22:55.874 --> 22:57.918
I would like to eat something good, too.

22:58.001 --> 22:59.294
Since Mr. Gojo is paying.

22:59.377 --> 23:01.713
Instant yakisoba
and yakisoba are different,

23:01.797 --> 23:03.715
and so are sushi and sushi train!

23:03.799 --> 23:05.425
I just want to eat sushi.

23:05.509 --> 23:07.928
Sushi is food
while sushi train is an entertainment!

23:08.011 --> 23:10.180
Like the difference
between theme parks and TDL!

23:10.263 --> 23:12.599
Also, Kugisaki,
you said you came from the boonies!

23:12.682 --> 23:14.434
-Have you ever had sushi train?
-What…

23:14.518 --> 23:16.478
My favorite is Sushi Go.

23:16.561 --> 23:18.480
But for starters, I'd go with Rippa Sushi.

23:18.563 --> 23:20.232
You're so knowledgeable, Mr. Gojo.

23:20.315 --> 23:21.441
We haven't decided yet.

23:21.525 --> 23:23.568
Kugisaki, listen up.

23:23.652 --> 23:24.945
At Rippa Sushi,

23:25.028 --> 23:27.948
the sushi will be delivered
on the bullet train.

23:28.031 --> 23:29.199
What?

23:29.282 --> 23:32.119
Driver, it's her first time
eating rotation sushi.

23:32.202 --> 23:35.872
Head to the Rippa Sushi outlet with a huge
parking lot along the national highway!
